```nix
{
  services.openssh = {
    enable = true;
    settings = {
      PasswordAuthentication = false;
      KbdInteractiveAuthentication = false;
      PubkeyAuthentication = true;
    };
  };

  # Make sure your user has a key registered:
  users.users.alice.openssh.authorizedKeys.keys = [
    "ssh-ed25519 AAAA... your-comment"
  ];
}
```

Key points:

- `PasswordAuthentication = false` is the switch that disables password logins; `KbdInteractiveAuthentication = false` closes the interactive (e.g. PAM) path too, since it can otherwise fall back to passwords.
