## Defining a systemd oneshot service in NixOS

In your NixOS configuration (e.g. `configuration.nix`):

```nix
{
  imports = [ ./hardware-configuration.nix ];

  services.bootScript = {
    description = "Run my script on boot";
    wanted = true;                       # enable at boot (default is true)
    path = [ pkgs.curl pkgs.jq ];        # binaries available in the service's PATH
    script = ''
      #!/usr/bin/env bash
      set -euo pipefail
      curl -s https://example.com/health > /var/log/boot-check.log
    '';
  };
}
```

Key points:

- **`systemd.services.<name>`** (or the alias `services.<name>`) defines a unit. Setting **`script`** makes it a **`Type=oneshot`** service by default — the unit runs the command once and is considered "active" when it finishes.
- **`wanted = true`** (the default) adds the unit to `multi-user.target`, so it starts at boot.
